gnome-shell-extension-lock-screen-suite (2.2.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Move the weather atmosphere into a bounded stage around the clock on
    the primary monitor: rain splashes on the clock cluster's roof and
    drips off its corners, snow settles and melts there, clouds drift
    behind it, fog gathers at its base. The animation pauses while the
    password prompt is up, and per-frame repainting is confined to the
    stage rectangle, fixing the wake-to-prompt lag of the full-screen
    version on multi-monitor setups.

 -- Norvi <apt@globalentry.systems>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

